    "input": "What documents do I need to open a savings account?",
    "response": "To open a savings account at VinBank, you typically need the following documents:\n\n**Required Documents:**\n- **Government-issued photo ID** (e.g., passport, driver's license, national ID card)\n- **Proof of address** (e.g., recent utility bill, bank statement, rental agreement)\n- **Social Security Number** (or equivalent identification number for your country)\n- **Phone number** and **email address** for account setup\n\n**Additional Information:**\n- Some accounts may require additional documentation depending on your location or specific account type\n- You might also need to complete identity verification through our online portal or visit a branch in person\n\nFor the most accurate and up-to-date requirements specific to your situation, I recommend visiting the VinBank website or contacting our customer service directly. They can provide detailed guidance tailored to your region and account preferences.\n\nIs there anything else I can help you with regarding your account?",
